# The source tree is somebody else's code, downloaded on demand and thrown away on
# demand. Tracking it would make our changes and upstream's indistinguishable, which
# is the exact failure the patches/ directory exists to avoid. Everything ignored
# here is regenerable from update + install; nothing ignored here is a source of truth.
source/
build/
files/
roms/
tmp

# Same reasoning one level down: the recipe for each outside library is tracked, the
# library's own source and the compiled result are not.
libs/source/
libs/prefix/

# Settings belong to whoever is sitting at the machine, not to the project. What is
# tracked is the fact that install creates them; what they end up saying is personal.
config/
config.ini
portable.ini
